TED (allocated == 0)\n- **Shipment quantity** - Stored in Shipment entity with default 1\n- **Shipment transitions** - Implemented: confirm (CREATED→CONFIRMED), deliver (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), cancel (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- **Pagination** - Implemented for all lists with limit (1-100, default 100), offset (0+, default 0), X-Total-Count header\n- **Fulfilment filter** - Implemented on GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS\n- **Customer check** - Implemented: orders for unknown customers rejected with 422 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\n- **Allocation constraint** - Implemented: POST /shipments rejects if allocated + new quantity &gt; order quantity with 409\n- **Quantity amendment** - Implemented: PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity sets quantity, rejected if below allocated quantity\n\n## Disagreed\n\nNo disagreement between planner's table and implementation. All computed values are calculated at read time from stored entities as specified.\n\n## Tests\n\n**New/modified test files:**\n\n1. **FulfilmentTest.kt** (14 tests) - Comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Order fulfilment status transitions (UNALLOCATED → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED → FULLY_ALLOCATED → DELIVERED)\n   - Multiple shipments accumulating allocated quantity\n   - Shipment delivery increasing delivered count\n   - Cancelled shipment releasing quantity\n   - New shipment acceptance after cancellation\n   - Quantity amendment changing fulfilment status\n   - All four fulfilment status filters\n   - Partial delivery scenarios\n\n2. **OrderControllerTest.kt** (12 tests, updated from baseline) - Now covers:\n   - Customer creation before order creation (new requirement)\n   - Quantity field in responses\n   - Fulfilment object in responses\n   - Pagination with limit, offset, X-Total-Count header\n   - Invalid pagination parameters (400)\n   - Fulfilment filter by status\n   - Invalid fulfilment status (400)\n   - Quantity amendment\n   - Quantity validation\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (13 tests, updated) - Now covers:\n   - Quantity field in shipments\n   - Pagination with X-Total-Count header\n   - Transition endpoints (confirm, deliver, cancel)\n   - Invalid transitions (409)\n   - Allocation constraint enforcement (409)\n   - Unknown shipment transitions (404)\n   - Shipment creation for non-existent orders (allowed)\n\n4. **CustomerControllerTest.kt** (5 tests, updated) - Now covers:\n   - Error envelope for unknown customer (404)\n   - Pagination with limit, offset, X-Total-Count header\n\n## Verification\n\nCommand: `./mvnw test` from `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/`\n\nResult: **BUILD SUCCESS** - All 45 tests pass (14 FulfilmentTest + 12 OrderControllerTest + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests + 13 ShipmentControllerTest + 5 CustomerControllerTest)\n\n## Not done\n\nAll requirements from BE-005 have been implemented:\n1. ✓ Partial fulfilment with quantity fields and allocation tracking\n2. ✓ Customer validation - orders for unknown customers rejected with 422\n3. ✓ Paged lists on all three endpoints with pagination parameters and X-Total-Count header\n4. ✓ Shipment transitions (confirm, deliver, cancel)\n5. ✓ Fulfilment status computation and filtering\n6. ✓ Quantity amendment endpoint\n7. ✓ Cancelled shipment quantity release\n8. ✓ Allocation constraint validation\n9. ✓ Error envelope consistency via 422 for unknown customers\n10. ✓ No new Maven dependencies added\n11. ✓ Tests updated to reflect new requirements"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2821,"cache_read_input_tokens":20965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2821},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c44d6de-0b17-43ec-8f31-47c64a720500","uuid":"3ac03cb0-8189-4cdf-931d-a9b6039a5a3c","timestamp":"2026-09-25T12:49:25.453Z","request_id":"req_011CfQBdk8hpUVCxqEmdkEVW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Esn4F1CJamptNLxxFijG3u":{"subagent_type":"verifier","description":"Verify BE-005 implementation","prompt":"# BE-005 — Partial fulfilment, customer check, paged lists\n\nThree changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n## Notes for the agent\n\nThe service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\nverify your work before finishing.\n\n---\n\n## PLANNER'S HANDOFF\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase and BE-005 ticket requirements, here is the comprehensive table of read paths:\n\n## Read paths\n\n| Read path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where computed |\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | orderId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | customerId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | amount | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | currency | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | quantity | Stored | Order entity (default 1 on creation) |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.allocated | Computed | Sum of non-CANCELLED shipment quantities for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.delivered | Computed | Sum of DELIVERED shipment quantities for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.status | Computed | Enum determined by: delivered == quantity → DELIVERED; allocated == quantity → FULLY_ALLOCATED; 0 &lt; allocated &lt; quantity → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED; allocated == 0 → UNALLOCATED |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].orderId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].customerId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].amount | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].currency | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].quantity | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].fulfilment.allocated | Computed | Sum of non-CANCELLED shipment quantities for each order |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].fulfilment.delivered | Computed | Sum of DELIVERED shipment quantities for each order |\n| GET /orders (list) | [].fulfilment.status | Computed | Enum per order based on allocated/delivered vs quantity |\n| GET /orders (list) | X-Total-Count header | Computed | Count of orders matching fulfilment filter (if provided), before limit/offset applied |\n| GET /orders?limit=N&amp;offset=M | order slice | Stored/Computed | Orders sorted by id, after applying fulfilment filter if present |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS | filtered list | Computed | Filter applied in repository query before pagination |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | orderId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | carrier | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | status | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | quantity | Stored | Shipment entity (default 1 on creation) |\n| GET /shipments (list) | [].shipmentId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments (list) | [].orderId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments (list) | [].carrier | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments (list) | [].status | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments (list) | [].quantity | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments (list) | X-Total-Count header | Computed | Total count of all shipments before limit/offset applied |\n| GET /shipments?limit=N&amp;offset=M | shipment slice | Stored | Shipments sorted by id |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | name | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | email | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers (list) | [].customerId | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers (list) | [].name | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers (list) | [].email | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers (list) | X-Total-Count header | Computed | Total count of all customers before limit/offset applied |\n| GET /customers?limit=N&amp;offset=M | customer slice | Stored | Customers sorted by id |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm | (entire Shipment response) | Stored | Shipment entity with status transitioned to CONFIRMED |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver | (entire Shipment response) | Stored | Shipment entity with status transitioned to DELIVERED |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel | (entire Shipment response) | Stored | Shipment entity with status transitioned to CANCELLED |\n| PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity | (entire Order response) | Stored/Computed | Order entity with updated quantity field; fulfilment recomputed with new quantity |\n\n## Shape\n\nValues are obtained through Spring Boot REST endpoints backed by in-memory repositories storing orders, shipments, and customers. Fulfillment status and allocations are computed on read by aggregating over related shipments; pagination totals are computed by counting filtered entities before slicing. Query parameters filter (fulfilment), order (id ascending), and slice (limit/offset) the lists. The X-Total-Count header reports count before slicing so clients can paginate efficiently.\n\n## Unresolved\n\nAll read paths above are fully resolvable as either stored in the in-memory repositories or computed from sums/enums over stored entities.\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTER'S HANDOFF\n\nPerfect! All tests pass. Let me now generate the final handoff summary.\n\n## Changed\n\n**Production files modified to implement BE-005:**\n\n1. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt` - Added quantity field (default 1) and Fulfilment object with allocated, delivered, and status fields\n2. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt` - Added quantity field (default 1) and DELIVERED status to ShipmentStatus enum\n3. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt` - Added quantity validation, customer existence check (422 for unknown customer), pagination (limit/offset/X-Total-Count), fulfilment filter, and quantity amendment endpoint\n4. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Added quantity validation, allocation constraint check on creation, shipment transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), and pagination\n5. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-b755f13f-34fb-405c-8667-ba8affab13a6/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt` - Changed to return error envelope via ResourceNotFoundException and added pagination\n6. `/pr