Shipment quantity** - Stored in Shipment entity with default 1\n- **Shipment transitions** - Implemented: confirm (CREATED→CONFIRMED), deliver (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), cancel (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- **Pagination** - Implemented for all lists with limit (1-100, default 100), offset (0+, default 0), X-Total-Count header\n- **Fulfilment filter** - Implemented on GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS\n- **Customer check** - Implemented: orders for unknown customers rejected with 422 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\n- **Allocation constraint** - Implemented: POST /shipments rejects if allocated + new quantity &gt; order quantity with 409\n- **Quantity amendment** - Implemented: PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity sets quantity, rejected if below allocated quantity\n\n## Disagreed\n\nNo disagreement between planner's table and implementation. All computed values are calculated at read time from stored entities as specified.\n\n## Tests\n\n**New/modified test files:**\n\n1. **FulfilmentTest.kt** (14 tests) - Comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Order fulfilment status transitions (UNALLOCATED → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED → FULLY_ALLOCATED → DELIVERED)\n   - Multiple shipments accumulating allocated quantity\n   - Shipment delivery increasing delivered count\n   - Cancelled shipment releasing quantity\n   - New shipment acceptance after cancellation\n   - Quantity amendment changing fulfilment status\n   - All four fulfilment status filters\n   - Partial delivery scenarios\n\n2. **OrderControllerTest.kt** (12 tests, updated from baseline) - Now covers:\n   - Customer creation before order creation (new requirement)\n   - Quantity field in responses\n   - Fulfilment object in responses\n   - Pagination with limit, offset, X-Total-Count header\n   - Invalid pagination parameters (400)\n   - Fulfilment filter by status\n   - Invalid fulfilment status (400)\n   - Quantity amendment\n   - Quantity validation\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (13 tests, updated) - Now covers:\n   - Quantity field in shipments\n   